WEBVTT


00:00:25.728 --> 00:00:28.196
Hey hey.
Hey, look.


00:00:30.333 --> 00:00:32.324
I need you to be strong
and stay with me


00:00:34.804 --> 00:00:37.204
because you're the one


00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:40.004
who's gonna have to kill me.


00:00:42.478 --> 00:00:44.844
(siren blaring)


00:00:45.948 --> 00:00:48.075
(horns honking)


00:00:56.592 --> 00:00:58.958
(heavy breathing)


00:01:09.739 --> 00:01:11.730
(phone ringing)


00:01:11.774 --> 00:01:15.175
Woman: Hey, honey.
I hate how we left things this morning.


00:01:15.211 --> 00:01:18.044
Maybe I'm just nervous
about my new show.


00:01:18.080 --> 00:01:19.308
I don't know.


00:01:21.183 --> 00:01:25.449
I know. My work is so much darker
than what I usually do


00:01:25.488 --> 00:01:28.116
and I don't know what people
are gonna think of it.


00:01:30.159 --> 00:01:32.320
It's just ever since I've been pregnant


00:01:32.361 --> 00:01:35.558
I have this feeling like I'm being
watched or followed.


00:01:41.537 --> 00:01:44.404
Yeah, I know what the books say.


00:01:44.440 --> 00:01:45.907
I don't know what it means.


00:01:45.942 --> 00:01:47.933
Maybe I'm just not ready
to be a mom.


00:01:50.579 --> 00:01:53.173
No, Jack, it's not
the hormones either.


00:01:53.215 --> 00:01:55.342
It feels different. Real.


00:01:55.384 --> 00:01:57.682
Like something's happening.


00:02:00.990 --> 00:02:04.357
Look, I'm going to the gallery to work
on something I've been thinking about.


00:02:04.393 --> 00:02:07.988
It's something I need
to get out of me.


00:02:09.031 --> 00:02:11.397
No, not the baby.


00:02:13.102 --> 00:02:16.128
I'll see you later.
Bye.


00:02:16.172 --> 00:02:18.436
(growling)


00:02:23.412 --> 00:02:25.710
(heavy breathing)


00:02:37.226 --> 00:02:39.091
- (metal scrapes)
- (gasps)


00:02:48.437 --> 00:02:50.496
(growling)


00:02:51.507 --> 00:02:53.304
Jack?


00:02:53.342 --> 00:02:55.207
Is that you?


00:03:00.316 --> 00:03:01.908
Hello?


00:03:01.951 --> 00:03:04.215
(metal clanking)


00:03:04.253 --> 00:03:06.619
Who's there?


00:03:11.260 --> 00:03:13.751
Man:
Hello, Kathryn.


00:03:13.796 --> 00:03:16.731
No. It's you.


00:03:16.766 --> 00:03:19.997
- Man: Yes.
- But...


00:03:21.003 --> 00:03:23.267
(screams)


00:03:24.974 --> 00:03:28.307
I've come for you
and what's inside of you.


00:03:28.344 --> 00:03:29.708
Kathryn: Oh my God


00:03:29.744 --> 00:03:33.578
Man:
The real evolution is coming.


00:03:33.615 --> 00:03:36.049
(Kathryn screams)


00:03:36.084 --> 00:03:38.917
No, not my baby.
Not my baby.


00:03:45.026 --> 00:03:47.460
- (growls)
- Baby.


00:03:48.830 --> 00:03:51.060
(gagging)


00:03:51.099 --> 00:03:53.465
(siren in distance)


00:04:04.546 --> 00:04:06.639
And now,


00:04:06.681 --> 00:04:08.911
18 years after the day I was born,


00:04:08.950 --> 00:04:11.885
I'm here to convince you
that the monsters are real,


00:04:11.920 --> 00:04:14.582
that they live among us,


00:04:16.424 --> 00:04:18.654
within us.


00:04:20.929 --> 00:04:23.397
And hopefully one day
you'll know who I was


00:04:24.833 --> 00:04:27.097
and what I tried to do.


00:04:29.037 --> 00:04:30.572
But for now...


00:04:30.572 --> 00:04:33.132
(alarm buzzing)


00:04:40.081 --> 00:04:42.379
Boy's voice:
Who am I?


00:04:43.585 --> 00:04:46.281
I guess I don't really have a good
answer to that question.


00:04:51.993 --> 00:04:53.585
Man:
Don't forget to take your pills.


00:04:53.628 --> 00:04:56.563
Boy's voice: I guess you already know
my mom died when I was born,


00:04:56.598 --> 00:04:58.998
but it never seemed like the end
of the world or anything.


00:04:59.033 --> 00:05:01.695
Is that weird?
Maybe.


00:05:01.736 --> 00:05:05.194
But how can you miss something
you never had, right?


00:05:05.240 --> 00:05:08.869
* The messages I left
weren't answered *


00:05:10.612 --> 00:05:13.706
* But I stayed off till bed *


00:05:13.748 --> 00:05:16.615
* These were the only
things I dreamt... *


00:05:16.651 --> 00:05:19.984
I know how to take an exam,
I know the periodic elements,


00:05:20.021 --> 00:05:22.080
I know how to do school.


00:05:22.123 --> 00:05:25.354
Do I have any idea
how to survive the real world?


00:05:26.394 --> 00:05:31.422
* So wake me when
the world's worth waking up for *


00:05:31.466 --> 00:05:35.527
* When my dreams don't stop
at my door *


00:05:35.570 --> 00:05:37.265
* When the world's worth... *


00:05:37.305 --> 00:05:39.432
My whole life I never
really felt like I fit in.


00:05:39.474 --> 00:05:41.965
I just watched people


00:05:42.010 --> 00:05:44.672
who looked like they were
actually enjoying their lives.


00:05:44.712 --> 00:05:47.203
Your final grades will be posted
tomorrow night


00:05:47.248 --> 00:05:50.217
outside the administration office
after graduation.


00:05:50.251 --> 00:05:53.186
Good luck. Your parents'
fading hopes and dreams


00:05:53.221 --> 00:05:55.314
are hanging on the outcome.


00:05:55.356 --> 00:05:57.153
Boy's voice:
And now graduation is almost here


00:05:57.192 --> 00:05:59.660
and I'm a little scared


00:05:59.694 --> 00:06:02.458
that everything is gonna change.


00:06:02.497 --> 00:06:04.897
Or even worse,


00:06:04.933 --> 00:06:07.527
that nothing's gonna change.


00:06:10.538 --> 00:06:12.529
I just thought you should know that


00:06:12.574 --> 00:06:15.338
before you waste any more
of your time on me.


00:06:15.376 --> 00:06:18.709
When I asked who you were,
I was looking for a name.


00:06:18.746 --> 00:06:20.646
Oh.


00:06:20.682 --> 00:06:23.310
Sorry.
Will Kidman.


00:06:23.351 --> 00:06:26.445
How is it possible
that in four years


00:06:26.487 --> 00:06:28.079
we haven't met until
your exit interview?


00:06:28.122 --> 00:06:30.818
Well, that's a good thing, right?


00:06:30.858 --> 00:06:33.349
That's one way to look at it.


00:06:35.063 --> 00:06:38.726
Oh, you were a part of
the debate team


00:06:38.766 --> 00:06:40.427
that brought home
the silver this year.


00:06:42.170 --> 00:06:44.866
A little disappointing, isn't it?


00:06:46.040 --> 00:06:48.838
You're obviously pretty bright


00:06:48.876 --> 00:06:52.710
and you appear
perfectly adequate on paper.


00:06:52.747 --> 00:06:56.239
It's just that there's
nothing special here.


00:06:58.286 --> 00:07:02.814
Four years, each day more impossibly
monotonous than the last.


00:07:02.857 --> 00:07:06.349
But after today, we'll never have to
walk down this awful hallway ever again.


00:07:06.394 --> 00:07:08.362
That's true, but soon
we'll have a whole lifetime


00:07:08.396 --> 00:07:10.864
of even longer and even more
depressing hallways after that.


00:07:10.898 --> 00:07:13.867
(chatting)


00:07:13.901 --> 00:07:15.732
So how many video yearbooks
have you sold so far?


00:07:15.770 --> 00:07:17.863
Two.


00:07:17.905 --> 00:07:20.169
I'm getting the impression that nobody
wants to relive high school


00:07:20.208 --> 00:07:22.472
in this sort of actual detail.


00:07:22.510 --> 00:07:25.001
But on a lighter note,


00:07:25.046 --> 00:07:29.676
I was finally able to hack into
the city's broadcast master control.


00:07:29.717 --> 00:07:31.241
What?


00:07:31.286 --> 00:07:33.117
I've got a computer loaded
and ready to go


00:07:33.154 --> 00:07:34.815
in the chapel
under construction upstairs.


00:07:34.856 --> 00:07:36.721
- Come here.
- Well...


00:07:36.758 --> 00:07:39.283
- What do you mean?
- It means that tomorrow,


00:07:39.327 --> 00:07:41.727
after my diploma is safely is hand,


00:07:41.763 --> 00:07:43.731
a backup generator will kick in


00:07:43.765 --> 00:07:47.064
and the regularly scheduled programming
of the greater metropolitan area


00:07:47.101 --> 00:07:49.569
will be preempted
by the world premiere


00:07:49.604 --> 00:07:52.630
of ''Untitled Sachin
Horror Project.''


00:07:52.674 --> 00:07:54.369
How do you even walk
with a pair that big?


00:07:54.409 --> 00:07:55.808
Like this.


00:07:55.843 --> 00:07:58.334
(girls laugh)


00:08:00.448 --> 00:08:02.575
High school girls are like
history class--


00:08:02.617 --> 00:08:05.450
completely fascinating
and utterly boring at the same time.


00:08:07.755 --> 00:08:09.450
Oh.


00:08:12.527 --> 00:08:14.825
Will: I mean, who even enrolls
their kids into a new school


00:08:14.862 --> 00:08:16.227
a month before graduation?


00:08:16.264 --> 00:08:18.960
Their parole officers.


00:08:35.650 --> 00:08:39.086
It's been four years, man.
It means your last chance.


00:08:40.655 --> 00:08:42.748
He who hesitates...


00:08:44.325 --> 00:08:45.656
Too much trouble.


00:08:45.693 --> 00:08:48.287
Yeah, Roland is kind of intimidating.


00:08:48.329 --> 00:08:49.853
But purely in a physical way.


00:08:49.897 --> 00:08:52.024
Will:
Not him. Her.


00:08:54.202 --> 00:08:56.636
Besides, I've got to worry about
getting into a good college.


00:08:56.671 --> 00:08:58.263
No time for distractions, right?


00:08:58.306 --> 00:08:59.933
(pounds locker)


00:09:04.245 --> 00:09:06.475
Uh, I-- I've--
I should go.


00:09:06.514 --> 00:09:08.277
Talk to you tomorrow!


00:09:11.419 --> 00:09:13.979
How many times
do I have to tell you?


00:09:14.021 --> 00:09:16.922
Elliana only dates within her species.
Understood?


00:09:16.958 --> 00:09:18.516
Will:
Understood.


00:09:18.559 --> 00:09:20.584
Please.


00:09:20.628 --> 00:09:23.153
If you get suspended before
the last day of school,


00:09:23.197 --> 00:09:25.131
who's gonna be my date
to the grad party?


00:09:25.166 --> 00:09:28.067
Go wait with the rest of the pack.
I'll be right there.


00:09:28.102 --> 00:09:31.196
You live for now.


00:09:38.645 --> 00:09:40.840
(chuckles nervously)


00:09:40.881 --> 00:09:42.712
No, I...


00:09:44.251 --> 00:09:46.776
I had him right where I wanted him,
but thanks.


00:09:48.488 --> 00:09:50.217
I'm Elliana.


00:09:52.159 --> 00:09:54.650
- You're Will.
- Yeah yeah, I am.


00:09:54.694 --> 00:09:57.060
So what do we have here?
May I?


00:10:07.007 --> 00:10:08.440
Why are they all of me?


00:10:11.378 --> 00:10:15.178
I guess there's nothing much else
interesting to draw around here.


00:10:16.983 --> 00:10:18.314
And I am?


00:10:24.157 --> 00:10:26.091
Sign it?


00:10:26.126 --> 00:10:27.718
Uh...


00:10:39.473 --> 00:10:41.703
There are two types
of people in the world:


00:10:41.741 --> 00:10:44.141
Those who take what they want,


00:10:45.579 --> 00:10:47.274
and those who get taken.


00:10:51.218 --> 00:10:53.152
Which are you, Will?


00:10:57.023 --> 00:10:58.547
(bell rings)


00:10:58.592 --> 00:11:00.082
Will's voice:
Fun science fact--


00:11:00.126 --> 00:11:02.117
what really separates humans
from other animals?


00:11:02.162 --> 00:11:05.154
2% of our DNA.
That's it.


00:11:11.137 --> 00:11:13.901
You okay?
You're bleeding.


00:11:13.940 --> 00:11:16.135
Oh yeah.
I'm fine, thanks.


00:11:16.176 --> 00:11:18.906
Hi, I'm Kay.


00:11:18.945 --> 00:11:21.379
Let me guess,


00:11:21.414 --> 00:11:23.279
your first fight.


00:11:23.316 --> 00:11:25.546
Yeah, but you should
see the other guy.


00:11:30.457 --> 00:11:32.254
He's perfectly fine.


00:11:35.428 --> 00:11:36.918
Don't worry.


00:11:36.963 --> 00:11:39.397
You'll have your revenge
in the real world.


00:11:39.432 --> 00:11:42.230
Guys like you eat guys
like him for lunch.


00:11:44.304 --> 00:11:47.865
I've got to go.
That one's mine.


00:11:47.908 --> 00:11:49.808
- Okay.
- Hang in there.


00:11:49.843 --> 00:11:52.539
Life gets better after high school.


00:11:54.281 --> 00:11:57.682
I promise.


00:11:57.717 --> 00:11:59.344
Thanks.


00:12:01.788 --> 00:12:04.256
(heavy breathing)


00:12:25.679 --> 00:12:29.547
Looking back, it's funny how days
just kind of blend together.


00:12:29.583 --> 00:12:32.245
One little unexpected moment


00:12:32.285 --> 00:12:34.344
can pretty much change everything.


00:12:34.387 --> 00:12:35.786
Jack:
What a shame.


00:12:35.822 --> 00:12:38.791
We didn't have to lock everything
down like that back in my day.


00:12:38.825 --> 00:12:41.350
(alarm blaring)


00:12:50.637 --> 00:12:52.332
Jack:
Happy birthday, Will.


00:12:54.741 --> 00:12:56.834
This used to be my favorite room
in the world.


00:12:56.876 --> 00:12:59.868
When your mom
was pregnant with you


00:12:59.913 --> 00:13:02.347
she'd come through that door,


00:13:02.382 --> 00:13:06.978
walk straight over here
and join me on this couch.


00:13:09.456 --> 00:13:11.549
She'd lay down,


00:13:11.591 --> 00:13:14.253
put her head on my lap


00:13:16.896 --> 00:13:18.955
and just talk,


00:13:18.999 --> 00:13:22.400
you know, about what
you might turn out like.


00:13:22.435 --> 00:13:24.801
Would you laugh like your mom


00:13:24.838 --> 00:13:26.738
or sigh like your old man?


00:13:26.773 --> 00:13:30.641
Or be some strange new combination
of the both of us?


00:13:33.980 --> 00:13:37.347
Used to be my favorite
room in the world.


00:13:38.685 --> 00:13:40.414
(sighs)
Now it's just a room.


00:13:45.425 --> 00:13:48.553
Your mom spent all the money
she had at the time to buy me this.


00:13:54.234 --> 00:13:56.327
A silver wedding band.


00:14:03.610 --> 00:14:05.840
I can't believe you finally took it off.


00:14:20.960 --> 00:14:22.188
Will’s voice:
I think it all comes down to this:


00:14:22.228 --> 00:14:24.458
The things we suppress


00:14:24.497 --> 00:14:26.761
very deep down in places
nobody can find them,


00:14:26.800 --> 00:14:28.665
they come back
and get us in the end...


00:14:29.869 --> 00:14:31.962
with a vengeance.


00:14:40.547 --> 00:14:44.574
It's funny, we take for granted
that we have free will,


00:14:44.617 --> 00:14:47.848
but we have so many rules
and expectations to live by.


00:14:47.887 --> 00:14:51.345
And if we didn't, we would all
probably just blindly follow


00:14:51.391 --> 00:14:53.791
our strongest desires,
good or bad, right?


00:14:55.995 --> 00:14:57.986
So where exactly is the free will?


00:15:16.750 --> 00:15:18.547
Okay.


00:15:18.585 --> 00:15:20.450
You can do this.


00:15:22.956 --> 00:15:24.787
Man:
Welcome to the party, Will.


00:15:24.824 --> 00:15:26.382
Will:
Thanks.


00:15:30.096 --> 00:15:31.791
I didn't even know
anything was down here.


00:15:31.831 --> 00:15:33.924
Where is everybody?


00:15:33.967 --> 00:15:38.097
Man: Don't worry.
It's a very exclusive guest list.


00:15:38.138 --> 00:15:40.902
(loud music playing)


00:15:42.508 --> 00:15:44.567
Whoa.


00:15:49.848 --> 00:15:52.442
Who are these people?
They aren't students.


00:15:53.719 --> 00:15:55.846
There are all kinds
of graduations, Will.


00:15:55.888 --> 00:15:59.153
Consider yourself special for being
the youngest guest invited.


00:15:59.191 --> 00:16:01.182
Stick out your tongue.


00:16:04.329 --> 00:16:07.492
Now say hello
like I taught you, pet.


00:16:16.108 --> 00:16:18.702
What-- what was that?


00:16:18.744 --> 00:16:21.212
Freedom.


00:16:22.548 --> 00:16:24.345
We got something else for you.


00:16:25.717 --> 00:16:27.378
She's yours, brother.


00:16:28.387 --> 00:16:29.911
Happy birthday.


00:16:32.591 --> 00:16:34.183
My plus one is here.


00:16:34.226 --> 00:16:36.694
Yeah.


00:16:36.728 --> 00:16:39.891
Me, here.


00:16:39.932 --> 00:16:43.390
I had a hunch there was something
behind that civilized exterior.


00:16:45.904 --> 00:16:48.737
- Let's dance.
- Oh no, I really don't do that.


00:16:55.247 --> 00:16:58.341
I have a feeling you're gonna be doing
all sorts of new things tonight.


00:17:07.893 --> 00:17:11.624
Can I ask you something?
Why Roland?


00:17:11.663 --> 00:17:14.393
Why not?


00:17:14.433 --> 00:17:17.368
Maybe because he has everything you
look for in a high school boyfriend--


00:17:17.402 --> 00:17:20.235
yummy face, nice ass,


00:17:20.272 --> 00:17:22.536
cool car,
chateau in the south of France.


00:17:22.574 --> 00:17:25.702
Oh, so it's a spiritual thing.


00:17:25.744 --> 00:17:27.803
He's a distraction.
Something for now.


00:17:27.846 --> 00:17:32.112
Besides, he's the one
who asked me out.


00:17:32.150 --> 00:17:34.710
I think most boys
are scared of me.


00:17:34.753 --> 00:17:37.688
So you've never been serious
about anyone?


00:17:37.723 --> 00:17:39.691
You mean in love.


00:17:41.026 --> 00:17:43.756
It's not like
I'm incapable of love, Will.


00:17:44.863 --> 00:17:47.730
I love the way this dress
hugs my ass.


00:17:50.269 --> 00:17:52.669
But commitment?
Well, let's just say


00:17:52.704 --> 00:17:54.604
it's more fun being free


00:17:54.640 --> 00:17:57.632
and a danger to myself
and others.


00:17:57.676 --> 00:17:59.667
(both laugh)


00:18:01.813 --> 00:18:03.804
Okay, my turn.


00:18:03.849 --> 00:18:06.340
You've drawn enough pictures
of me to fill a gallery.


00:18:06.385 --> 00:18:09.411
So why is it we've never had
a real conversation until this moment?


00:18:09.454 --> 00:18:13.151
The accepted social order
of high school, I guess.


00:18:13.191 --> 00:18:16.217
Where do you fit into
the accepted social order?


00:18:16.261 --> 00:18:18.092
I don't know.


00:18:18.130 --> 00:18:21.827
I just kind of blend into my
environment, avoid the predators.


00:18:21.867 --> 00:18:23.732
What are you so scared of?


00:18:26.939 --> 00:18:30.272
- You, mostly.
- Well, don't worry.


00:18:30.309 --> 00:18:32.300
I don't bite...


00:18:33.312 --> 00:18:35.337
much.


00:18:38.817 --> 00:18:40.785
(laughs)


00:18:50.195 --> 00:18:52.220
(growling)


00:18:52.264 --> 00:18:53.822
What's wrong?


00:18:53.865 --> 00:18:56.356
I don't know.
I feel weird.


00:18:56.401 --> 00:18:58.426
Someone gave me a pill earlier.


00:18:58.470 --> 00:19:01.303
- (laughs)
- (woman screams)


00:19:01.340 --> 00:19:03.774
Just roll with it.


00:19:03.809 --> 00:19:06.277
- (growling)
- (woman screaming)


00:19:06.311 --> 00:19:07.778
Where's my glasses?
What's going on?


00:19:07.813 --> 00:19:10.714
Come on, Will.
Let go. Let it happen.


00:19:12.084 --> 00:19:13.745
We've got to go.
We've got to go.


00:19:13.785 --> 00:19:16.151
- No, it's just getting good.
- Come on.


00:19:17.656 --> 00:19:20.750
I think I'm seeing things.
Well, like--


00:19:20.792 --> 00:19:23.454
Let's just get some fresh air.


00:19:27.466 --> 00:19:29.297
Do you remember
where the exit was?


00:19:29.334 --> 00:19:31.598
(banging)


00:19:32.671 --> 00:19:34.468
Elliana?


00:19:39.044 --> 00:19:41.069
Elliana, is that you?


00:19:42.247 --> 00:19:44.272
(growls)


00:19:46.952 --> 00:19:49.182
What is that?
What is that?


00:19:51.590 --> 00:19:54.423
Elliana, can you hear me?


00:19:54.459 --> 00:19:56.324
(growling continues)


00:20:07.272 --> 00:20:08.933
(thuds)


00:20:11.443 --> 00:20:13.934
- (growling)
- (pounding)


00:20:19.117 --> 00:20:20.846
Where's the door?


00:20:25.157 --> 00:20:26.624
- (growling)
- (pounding)


00:20:36.034 --> 00:20:37.968
(grunts)


00:20:47.112 --> 00:20:49.046
Whoa whoa whoa.


00:20:49.081 --> 00:20:51.447
What the hell are you doing?


00:20:51.483 --> 00:20:53.747
There's something down there, okay?
There's something down there.


00:20:53.785 --> 00:20:55.548
Something, huh?


00:20:55.587 --> 00:20:57.418
It's attacking people
and it's not human.


00:20:57.456 --> 00:20:59.390
Not human, huh?


00:20:59.424 --> 00:21:03.485
Fill that out and under


00:21:03.528 --> 00:21:06.361
''Perpetrator ethnicity''


00:21:06.398 --> 00:21:08.195
put ''Other.''


00:21:08.233 --> 00:21:10.360
Will?


00:21:10.402 --> 00:21:12.996
Elliana?


00:21:13.038 --> 00:21:15.700
Are you okay?


00:21:15.740 --> 00:21:17.674
But...


00:21:17.709 --> 00:21:19.802
How did you--
how did--


00:21:21.613 --> 00:21:23.274
Jesus, kid.


00:21:23.315 --> 00:21:26.751
You're high as a kite, aren't you?
You with him?


00:21:26.785 --> 00:21:28.753
No.


00:21:29.788 --> 00:21:31.483
No.


00:21:36.294 --> 00:21:38.194
Will’s voice:
Today was not at all what I expected


00:21:38.230 --> 00:21:39.754
when I woke up this morning.


00:21:39.798 --> 00:21:42.528
But the days that change
your life forever rarely are.


00:21:45.137 --> 00:21:46.900
Will:
This is gonna be really awkward,


00:21:46.938 --> 00:21:49.428
but I need to talk to you
about something.


00:21:49.473 --> 00:21:51.805
Okay, please don't tell me


00:21:51.842 --> 00:21:54.208
that you've secretly been
in love with me all these years.


00:21:54.245 --> 00:21:56.338
- No.
- Oh.


00:21:56.380 --> 00:21:59.213
Well, then please carry on.
And here, make yourself useful.


00:22:01.252 --> 00:22:03.186
What can you tell me about--


00:22:06.390 --> 00:22:08.688
what can you tell me
about werewolves?


00:22:08.726 --> 00:22:13.095
Well, considering that three
of my 1 2 unproduced screenplays


00:22:13.130 --> 00:22:17.658
involve lycanthropes of some variety,
I can tell you a lot.


00:22:17.701 --> 00:22:19.635
Okay, they don't like
silver bullets, right?


00:22:20.638 --> 00:22:23.163
No, they don't like any silver
in their bloodstream


00:22:23.207 --> 00:22:24.834
to the point of dying from it.


00:22:24.875 --> 00:22:29.175
And the only other way a human can kill
a run-of-the-mill werewolf is by fire.


00:22:29.213 --> 00:22:31.909
Have you never seen
a werewolf flick?


00:22:31.949 --> 00:22:34.440
Eh, can't blame you.


00:22:34.485 --> 00:22:37.420
That's what studios get for casting
geezers in their lead roles.


00:22:37.454 --> 00:22:39.115
I mean, if I want to see
people in their 40s


00:22:39.156 --> 00:22:40.555
I would just go home
and look at my parents.


00:22:40.591 --> 00:22:43.924
Okay, this is just gonna
sound crazy,


00:22:43.961 --> 00:22:47.727
but I maybe saw one
at the party last night.


00:22:47.765 --> 00:22:51.929
Okay, the party where I assume
it was wild and dark


00:22:51.969 --> 00:22:54.335
and you were high on drugs?


00:22:55.706 --> 00:22:57.071
Yeah.


00:23:01.879 --> 00:23:03.574
So silver and fire, that's it?


00:23:03.614 --> 00:23:07.106
Will, these aren't your
makeup-wearing, skin-glistening


00:23:07.151 --> 00:23:09.415
pansy-ass vampires, okay?


00:23:09.453 --> 00:23:12.445
There's not some grocery list
of items that you can just get


00:23:12.489 --> 00:23:15.117
to cripple them
or scare them off like,


00:23:15.159 --> 00:23:19.459
''Oh, garlic.
Oh, some holy water.''


00:23:19.496 --> 00:23:22.522
You know, two fingers
perpendicular to each other.


00:23:32.343 --> 00:23:35.506
Okay, look. Real lycanthropes
are hard-frickin'-core.


00:23:35.546 --> 00:23:38.310
Okay? They're doomed to struggle
between their humanity


00:23:38.349 --> 00:23:40.840
and their animal natures.
And once they kill a human,


00:23:40.884 --> 00:23:44.581
which they like always do,
there's no going back.


00:23:44.622 --> 00:23:47.386
They become vicious killers for life.


00:23:49.526 --> 00:23:52.324
So hypothetically, there wouldn't
be anything to worry about


00:23:52.363 --> 00:23:54.388
'cause there's already a full moon
this month, right?


00:23:54.431 --> 00:23:57.696
There's a full moon tonight.
A blue moon, actually.


00:23:57.735 --> 00:24:01.136
So if they were really out there,


00:24:01.171 --> 00:24:04.334
that should certainly kick things
up a notch, wouldn't it?


00:24:06.844 --> 00:24:08.505
Why would they be after me?


00:24:08.545 --> 00:24:12.140
Either you pose a threat
to their existence


00:24:12.182 --> 00:24:13.809
or you're food.


00:24:16.787 --> 00:24:18.618
In your case,


00:24:18.656 --> 00:24:20.920
I'm guessing they've already
picked out the best wine


00:24:20.958 --> 00:24:22.448
to bring out your flavor.


00:24:24.828 --> 00:24:27.160
What are they doing in here?


00:24:27.197 --> 00:24:30.724
Well, nobody goes
to church anymore,


00:24:30.768 --> 00:24:33.293
so this is gonna be
the new computer lab.


00:24:35.139 --> 00:24:37.437
You know, when somebody had
a question they couldn't answer,


00:24:37.474 --> 00:24:40.409
they used to ask God.
Now they ask Wikipedia.


00:24:40.444 --> 00:24:42.309
(laughs)


00:24:42.346 --> 00:24:44.780
The god with answers.


00:24:46.517 --> 00:24:48.610
(bell rings)


00:25:01.198 --> 00:25:03.598
* When he moves I watch him
from behind *


00:25:03.634 --> 00:25:05.431
* He turns and laughter
flickers in his eyes *


00:25:05.469 --> 00:25:07.596
* Intent and direct
when he speaks *


00:25:07.638 --> 00:25:09.128
* I watch his lips *


00:25:09.173 --> 00:25:11.368
* And when he drives
I love to watch his hands *


00:25:11.408 --> 00:25:13.569
* White and smooth,
almost feminine *


00:25:13.610 --> 00:25:15.134
* Almost American *


00:25:15.179 --> 00:25:17.204
- * I have to watch him... *
- (phone vibrating)


00:25:17.247 --> 00:25:19.408
* In his face age descends on youth *


00:25:19.450 --> 00:25:21.350
* Exaggeration on the truth *


00:25:21.385 --> 00:25:25.378
* He caught me looking in then,
but soon his eyes forgot me *


00:25:25.422 --> 00:25:29.290
* And everything he seems to do
reflects just another shade of blue *


00:25:29.326 --> 00:25:32.261
* I saw him searching into you
and ached a while *


00:25:32.296 --> 00:25:34.856
* I watch his lips caress the glass *


00:25:34.898 --> 00:25:37.264
* His fingers stroke
its stem and pass *


00:25:37.301 --> 00:25:39.030
* To lift a cigarette at last *


00:25:39.069 --> 00:25:43.233
* He dries his eyes
from a shadow by the stair *


00:25:43.273 --> 00:25:44.706
* I watch as he weeps unaware *


00:25:44.742 --> 00:25:46.539
* That I'm in awe of his despair *


00:25:48.846 --> 00:25:50.905
* In his face
age descends on youth *


00:25:50.948 --> 00:25:52.540
* Exaggeration on the truth *


00:25:52.583 --> 00:25:56.041
* He caught me looking in then,
but soon his eyes forgot me *


00:25:56.086 --> 00:25:59.078
* And everything he seems to do *


00:25:59.123 --> 00:26:00.818
* Reflects just another
shade of blue *


00:26:00.858 --> 00:26:03.258
* I saw him searching into you
and ached a while *


00:26:03.293 --> 00:26:06.660
* In his face age descends on youth *


00:26:06.697 --> 00:26:08.460
* Exaggeration on the truth *


00:26:08.499 --> 00:26:11.593
* He caught me looking in then,
but soon his eyes forgot me *


00:26:11.635 --> 00:26:14.832
* And everything he seems to do *


00:26:14.872 --> 00:26:16.965
* Reflects just another
shade of blue *


00:26:17.007 --> 00:26:20.374
* I saw him searching into you
and ached a while... *


00:26:43.834 --> 00:26:46.667
(bell rings)


00:26:46.703 --> 00:26:48.466
Woman on P.A.:
Last ever school lunch


00:26:48.505 --> 00:26:51.235
now being served, seniors.


00:26:55.179 --> 00:26:57.204
(door squeaks)


00:27:00.050 --> 00:27:02.575
Was I not clear with you, man?


00:27:02.619 --> 00:27:05.486
Were you seriously with
Elliana last night?


00:27:05.522 --> 00:27:08.719
School's almost over.
Just leave me alone.


00:27:08.759 --> 00:27:11.319
- I'm never gonna see her again.
- That's not good enough, man.


00:27:12.796 --> 00:27:14.889
Hey, what do you think
you're doing?


00:27:17.100 --> 00:27:19.000
Right now, looking at an asshole.


00:27:20.771 --> 00:27:24.138
Well, there must be something
wrong with your glasses.


00:27:24.174 --> 00:27:25.937
(cracks)


00:27:25.976 --> 00:27:28.274
Oh, that's it.


00:27:28.312 --> 00:27:30.371
They're broken.


00:27:32.649 --> 00:27:34.207
This is where you die, man.


00:27:34.251 --> 00:27:36.549
And nobody's around to save
your sorry ass this time.


00:27:37.888 --> 00:27:39.617
(grunting)


00:27:44.862 --> 00:27:46.727
(growls)


00:28:07.383 --> 00:28:09.578
(panting)


00:28:24.233 --> 00:28:26.292
I'm gonna tear you up, Kidman.


00:28:55.464 --> 00:28:57.022
Where are you, Kidman?


00:29:00.970 --> 00:29:03.131
Hey, I just want to talk.


00:29:12.715 --> 00:29:14.478
You're dead.


00:29:16.719 --> 00:29:18.516
(growling)


00:29:19.689 --> 00:29:21.418
Oh crap.


00:29:21.457 --> 00:29:23.448
- (roaring)
- Fuck!


00:29:23.492 --> 00:29:25.517
Hey, what the hell are you?


00:29:28.698 --> 00:29:30.495
(gunshots)


00:29:34.737 --> 00:29:36.932
Hey, I'm not an asshole, man.


00:29:36.973 --> 00:29:38.702
I'm just misunderstood.


00:29:38.741 --> 00:29:41.266
Okay okay, I am an asshole.


00:29:43.212 --> 00:29:45.009
- Please don't hurt me.
- (roars)


00:29:45.047 --> 00:29:48.039
(screaming)


00:29:51.187 --> 00:29:53.255
(heavy breathing)


00:30:00.830 --> 00:30:03.162
Will’s voice:
You know what we do?


00:30:03.199 --> 00:30:05.565
We let moments pass,
opportunities pass,


00:30:05.601 --> 00:30:07.694
our lives pass,


00:30:07.737 --> 00:30:10.103
day after day


00:30:10.139 --> 00:30:12.369
until before we know it,
without even realizing it,


00:30:12.408 --> 00:30:15.172
the best versions of ourselves
have become a distant memory.


00:30:17.847 --> 00:30:19.781
Look, I've been going
through life on autopilot


00:30:19.815 --> 00:30:21.339
with nothing really required of me--


00:30:21.384 --> 00:30:24.148
stop, go, do this,
don't do that,


00:30:24.186 --> 00:30:27.246
moving along being polite,
just surviving.


00:30:29.225 --> 00:30:31.386
I don't want to be one
of the herd anymore.


00:30:31.427 --> 00:30:33.759
What do you want, Will?


00:30:41.003 --> 00:30:46.532
* Nothing you do can stop me
from living today *


00:30:49.779 --> 00:30:53.545
* Nothing you say
can keep me down *


00:30:53.582 --> 00:30:56.642
* I'm on my way *


00:30:59.155 --> 00:31:00.850
* What will you scream... *


00:31:00.890 --> 00:31:03.324
I want you.


00:31:04.794 --> 00:31:07.194
I've wanted to say that
for a really long time.


00:31:18.107 --> 00:31:19.870
Nice ass.


00:31:34.323 --> 00:31:35.654
What smells so good?


00:31:35.691 --> 00:31:38.319
Graduation dogs.
You want me to hook you up?


00:31:40.529 --> 00:31:42.292
Yeah, I really do,


00:31:42.331 --> 00:31:44.856
but no thanks.
I don't eat meat.


00:31:44.900 --> 00:31:47.334
You have any idea what
they put in these things?


00:31:47.369 --> 00:31:49.269
I wouldn't exactly call it meat.


00:31:50.906 --> 00:31:54.672
Come on, live a little.


00:31:59.448 --> 00:32:02.110
Why not?
Yeah, give me one with everything.


00:32:17.533 --> 00:32:19.797
(crunches)


00:32:26.408 --> 00:32:29.070
So, did you have fun
at the party last night?


00:32:30.246 --> 00:32:32.237
(crunches)


00:32:37.787 --> 00:32:39.652
How does Roland taste?


00:32:42.858 --> 00:32:44.985
Oh my-- oh my God.


00:32:45.027 --> 00:32:47.086
(coughing, vomiting)


00:32:47.129 --> 00:32:49.063
(students murmuring)


00:32:53.936 --> 00:32:57.133
Have you been experiencing any
other unusual symptoms lately?


00:32:57.173 --> 00:33:00.074
(sighs)
You wouldn't believe me.


00:33:00.109 --> 00:33:02.134
Some really crazy shit's been going on.


00:33:02.178 --> 00:33:04.043
Hmm.


00:33:04.079 --> 00:33:05.910
Well, you're at
the tail end of puberty


00:33:05.948 --> 00:33:08.416
and you're under
the stress of final exams,


00:33:08.450 --> 00:33:10.213
worried about going to college.


00:33:10.252 --> 00:33:12.743
It's perfectly normal.


00:33:12.788 --> 00:33:14.949
District requires us to draw blood


00:33:14.990 --> 00:33:18.187
just to verify that it's not a virus
or drugs.


00:33:18.227 --> 00:33:20.787
But I'm sure you
and your blood are just fine.


00:33:29.972 --> 00:33:31.940
(coins clinking)


00:33:33.042 --> 00:33:35.476
(machine humming)


00:33:38.113 --> 00:33:40.445
Damn it!


00:33:40.482 --> 00:33:43.610
I saw the whole thing.
That Javamatic had it coming.


00:33:51.694 --> 00:33:53.753
Do I know you from somewhere?


00:33:55.831 --> 00:33:58.425
I don't think so.


00:33:58.467 --> 00:34:00.332
My name is Kay.


00:34:00.369 --> 00:34:02.268
Jack.


00:34:02.303 --> 00:34:05.136
I'd shake, but I think I might
have broke my hand.


00:34:11.846 --> 00:34:13.313
So what brings you here?


00:34:13.348 --> 00:34:15.475
My boy.


00:34:15.516 --> 00:34:18.610
Me too.
Must be the full moon or something.


00:34:18.653 --> 00:34:21.588
I just-- it's getting
so hard, you know?


00:34:21.623 --> 00:34:23.454
You just want to protect them.


00:34:23.491 --> 00:34:27.484
I had him strapped in a car seat
till he was eight.


00:34:27.528 --> 00:34:28.995
Hmm.


00:34:29.030 --> 00:34:30.554
Today you got child-proof cabinets,


00:34:30.598 --> 00:34:32.964
flame-retardant pajamas,


00:34:33.001 --> 00:34:35.561
- bicycle helmets.
- Hmm.


00:34:35.603 --> 00:34:37.798
The closest thing I had
to a bicycle helmet


00:34:37.839 --> 00:34:39.704
was when I grew my hair out
in the eighth grade.


00:34:42.010 --> 00:34:44.240
There's some things
you can't protect them from


00:34:44.279 --> 00:34:45.871
no matter how hard you try.


00:34:49.217 --> 00:34:51.378
Yeah, like from girls.


00:34:52.654 --> 00:34:54.178
End up breaking their heart.


00:34:54.222 --> 00:34:56.213
Well, you know
my philosophy on that is


00:34:56.257 --> 00:34:59.818
kill the first one who does
and hope that the word gets around.


00:34:59.861 --> 00:35:01.158
(laughs)


00:35:03.665 --> 00:35:06.156
Hey, what's the emergency?


00:35:06.200 --> 00:35:08.327
How do you become a werewolf?


00:35:08.369 --> 00:35:10.496
All right, what is going on with you?


00:35:10.538 --> 00:35:13.837
Now I'm glad that you've become a fan.
I really am.


00:35:13.875 --> 00:35:16.435
But you're verging on
major geekdom here.


00:35:16.477 --> 00:35:18.001
Humor me, please.


00:35:19.213 --> 00:35:23.115
Okay. If a werewolf
drew blood from you


00:35:23.151 --> 00:35:27.053
and you survive,
then you would become one.


00:35:28.122 --> 00:35:30.420
- Did that happen?
- I don't know.


00:35:31.659 --> 00:35:34.594
How would I find out?
You know, like hypothetically?


00:35:34.629 --> 00:35:37.257
- Dude, have you been working out?
- Dude!


00:35:37.298 --> 00:35:39.596
Sorry. Yeah, no,
hypothetically,


00:35:39.634 --> 00:35:42.831
um, you could use one of these


00:35:42.870 --> 00:35:44.963
and try and kill yourself.


00:35:45.006 --> 00:35:47.065
Your wounds would heal.


00:35:47.108 --> 00:35:49.804
Remember, only fire and silver


00:35:49.844 --> 00:35:53.302
can kill a garden variety
lycanthrope.


00:35:53.348 --> 00:35:55.077
Garden variety lycanthrope?


00:35:55.116 --> 00:35:57.107
Yeah, as opposed to the alpha,


00:35:57.151 --> 00:36:00.552
the leader,
the uberwolf.


00:36:01.589 --> 00:36:03.523
No one really knows how
you become one,


00:36:03.558 --> 00:36:06.994
but if you are one,
only another wolf can kill you.


00:36:07.028 --> 00:36:09.428
(laughs)
But no other wolf would have the balls.


00:36:11.299 --> 00:36:12.789
What do you say
we test your theory?


00:36:12.834 --> 00:36:15.928
Well, I guess I should go
check on mine.


00:36:19.574 --> 00:36:21.906
Um,


00:36:21.943 --> 00:36:25.902
would you like to get lunch
or maybe drinks this afternoon?


00:36:25.947 --> 00:36:28.279
I could really use one.


00:36:30.051 --> 00:36:31.746
Thanks.


00:36:31.786 --> 00:36:34.277
But I think I've had enough excitement
for one day.


00:36:34.322 --> 00:36:36.051
Okay.


00:36:36.090 --> 00:36:39.526
Well, I'll be at Bradner's Pub
in case you change your mind.


00:36:41.963 --> 00:36:43.294
Maybe I will.


00:36:47.201 --> 00:36:48.930
What are you, insane?


00:36:48.970 --> 00:36:53.532
Look, you're not a werewolf, okay?


00:36:53.574 --> 00:36:55.667
Your wounds will not heal.


00:36:57.111 --> 00:36:59.204
Okay, wait wait.
What are you--


00:36:59.247 --> 00:37:01.078
Okay, what if something
goes wrong?


00:37:01.115 --> 00:37:03.310
What am I supposed to tell
the authorities?


00:37:03.351 --> 00:37:05.478
Okay, wait wait.


00:37:08.990 --> 00:37:11.356
You know, just in case.


00:37:21.836 --> 00:37:23.235
(groans)


00:37:25.306 --> 00:37:27.069
(groans)


00:37:27.108 --> 00:37:28.803
- (scalpel clangs)
- Sachin: Oh oh shit.


00:37:28.843 --> 00:37:31.573
Oh shit.
Um, okay.


00:37:31.612 --> 00:37:33.876
Uh, oh man.


00:37:33.915 --> 00:37:37.214
When you play a practical joke
you really commit.


00:37:37.251 --> 00:37:39.617
Okay, I'm gonna go get the nurse.


00:37:56.771 --> 00:37:59.433
What the hell
is happening to me?!


00:38:14.889 --> 00:38:16.789
Lycanthrope.


00:38:21.729 --> 00:38:23.128
(gasps)


00:38:23.164 --> 00:38:24.825
Four years of high school
finally over


00:38:24.866 --> 00:38:27.300
and you celebrate
by coming to the library.


00:38:34.909 --> 00:38:36.934
You look yummy.


00:38:36.978 --> 00:38:39.742
I'm pretty sure all of the E
from last night


00:38:39.780 --> 00:38:43.375
is out of my system by now,
so why?


00:38:45.653 --> 00:38:47.883
This is gonna sound


00:38:47.922 --> 00:38:49.890
so stupid.


00:38:51.692 --> 00:38:53.956
But...


00:38:55.930 --> 00:38:58.592
I think that I might be...


00:39:00.501 --> 00:39:02.093
a werewolf.


00:39:06.774 --> 00:39:10.107
Will’s voice:
Vampires, they've got it easy.


00:39:11.412 --> 00:39:13.471
They're all about wish fulfillment.


00:39:13.514 --> 00:39:15.641
Me? I can't read minds.


00:39:15.683 --> 00:39:18.550
I'm not really older and wiser
and more mature than I look.


00:39:18.586 --> 00:39:22.044
Well, we do have half an hour
before they lock down campus.


00:39:22.089 --> 00:39:24.557
You want to find out?


00:39:24.592 --> 00:39:26.526
Will’s voice:
I'm just a guy


00:39:26.561 --> 00:39:29.621
who wants to do
really bad things to a girl.


00:39:29.664 --> 00:39:32.827
(horns honking)


00:39:32.867 --> 00:39:35.131
(laughing)


00:39:35.169 --> 00:39:39.037
I knew you'd join me
for a drink, or five.


00:39:39.073 --> 00:39:40.802
You did, huh?


00:39:49.951 --> 00:39:52.681
Aw. A cutie.


00:39:52.720 --> 00:39:56.622
Look, I know that there's this
whole courtship ritual thing


00:39:56.657 --> 00:39:58.921
I'm supposed to follow, but--


00:39:58.960 --> 00:40:01.986
Well, how about we skip
the clumsy first date


00:40:02.029 --> 00:40:04.054
where you don't even know
if it's okay to kiss me


00:40:04.098 --> 00:40:08.033
because really you're not even sure
we're actually on a date?


00:40:13.974 --> 00:40:15.635
And while we're at it,


00:40:15.675 --> 00:40:18.974
why don't we skip the more
promising second date


00:40:19.012 --> 00:40:21.913
where I've proven to you


00:40:21.948 --> 00:40:24.178
what a good listener I am,


00:40:24.217 --> 00:40:27.584
but really all I'm thinking about


00:40:27.621 --> 00:40:30.886
is what sex with you
would be like?


00:40:30.924 --> 00:40:33.017
Okay. While we're at it


00:40:33.059 --> 00:40:36.222
maybe we should
just skip the third date too


00:40:36.263 --> 00:40:39.198
where we have really bad sex.


00:40:39.232 --> 00:40:41.257
Well, in that case,


00:40:41.301 --> 00:40:43.531
let's pretend
this is the fourth date.


00:40:43.570 --> 00:40:47.062
And if we don't have sex again soon,


00:40:47.107 --> 00:40:50.474
and if it's not really good this time,


00:40:50.510 --> 00:40:53.604
things are gonna get awkward
between us.


00:40:53.647 --> 00:40:55.342
Do you trust me?


00:41:00.920 --> 00:41:02.683
I'll take that as a yes.


00:41:03.790 --> 00:41:05.382
You see, in the movies


00:41:05.425 --> 00:41:08.553
the concerned friend always handcuffs
the possible werewolf


00:41:08.595 --> 00:41:12.224
to keep him from harming anyone
in case he turns.


00:41:18.204 --> 00:41:19.694
This will have to do.


00:41:32.085 --> 00:41:33.746
Where did you come from?


00:41:35.288 --> 00:41:37.779
The better question is,


00:41:37.824 --> 00:41:39.587
where have I been?


00:41:39.626 --> 00:41:43.187
(laughs)
What are you talking about?


00:41:45.799 --> 00:41:48.063
Now,


00:41:48.101 --> 00:41:50.968
let's see if you made
the right choice.


00:41:56.242 --> 00:41:58.972
Because if you're a werewolf,


00:41:59.012 --> 00:42:02.778
then I may have just saved
some innocent lives.


00:42:04.451 --> 00:42:06.214
(zipper unzips)


00:42:06.252 --> 00:42:09.221
But if I'm a werewolf,


00:42:09.255 --> 00:42:13.919
then you just made
a very very bad mistake.


00:42:17.731 --> 00:42:20.222
You're completely at my mercy.


00:42:29.442 --> 00:42:31.569
(deep moan)


00:42:31.611 --> 00:42:33.476
Ah.


00:42:38.618 --> 00:42:41.018
(both laugh)


00:42:43.223 --> 00:42:46.715
Now I think you should just stay
there and cool down a bit


00:42:46.760 --> 00:42:48.819
'cause it looks like
you're going through


00:42:48.862 --> 00:42:50.659
a little transformation right now.


00:42:50.697 --> 00:42:52.392
(laughs)


00:42:57.036 --> 00:42:59.095
(sighs)


00:42:59.139 --> 00:43:01.403
- So you're not--
- A monster?


00:43:01.441 --> 00:43:04.569
No. Not literally anyway.


00:43:06.980 --> 00:43:08.971
I'm gonna go out on a limb


00:43:09.015 --> 00:43:11.108
and say that neither are you.


00:43:14.654 --> 00:43:17.987
Aren't you even a little curious
why this is happening?


00:43:18.024 --> 00:43:20.322
Why I'm here with you?


00:43:20.360 --> 00:43:22.555
Oh, come on, Jack.


00:43:22.595 --> 00:43:25.621
I know I'm bigger, stronger,


00:43:25.665 --> 00:43:28.498
cut off that wispy red hair.


00:43:28.535 --> 00:43:32.232
I stayed young and beautiful
while you just grew old.


00:43:32.272 --> 00:43:35.173
But you wore my ring
for 20 years


00:43:35.208 --> 00:43:37.733
- till last night, baby.
- (gasps)


00:43:41.014 --> 00:43:43.175
What's the matter?


00:43:43.216 --> 00:43:45.013
You look like you've seen a ghost.


00:43:45.051 --> 00:43:46.882
What's happening?


00:43:51.257 --> 00:43:54.658
You were so worried
about keeping our boy safe,


00:43:54.694 --> 00:43:57.629
you didn't even give him the tools
to take care of himself.


00:43:57.664 --> 00:43:59.962
Now I have to do it.


00:44:02.001 --> 00:44:03.593
Don't you remember?


00:44:04.637 --> 00:44:07.128
Till death do us part.


00:44:07.173 --> 00:44:09.437
(roaring)


00:44:09.476 --> 00:44:11.774
- (Jack screaming)
- (school bell ringing)


00:44:12.946 --> 00:44:14.573
(students shouting, chatting)


00:44:14.614 --> 00:44:17.105
Man on P.A.: Enjoy your summer.
Good luck, graduates.


00:44:26.092 --> 00:44:28.890
Who did that to you?


00:44:28.928 --> 00:44:31.795
I don't know.


00:44:31.831 --> 00:44:33.799
When they killed my mom
they got me too.


00:44:34.934 --> 00:44:37.459
* You don't need to change *


00:44:37.504 --> 00:44:39.495
* A thing about you, babe *


00:44:39.539 --> 00:44:41.666
* I'm telling you,
from where I sit *


00:44:41.708 --> 00:44:42.970
* You're one of a kind... *


00:44:43.009 --> 00:44:44.670
When I was 1 2


00:44:44.711 --> 00:44:46.770
my mom and I came home
from this day of shopping


00:44:46.813 --> 00:44:48.610
to find half of our stuff gone--


00:44:48.648 --> 00:44:51.412
furniture, TVs-- whatever.


00:44:51.451 --> 00:44:53.510
I thought we'd been robbed.


00:44:55.188 --> 00:44:56.815
(sighs)
You weren't?


00:44:56.856 --> 00:44:59.154
My dad left us.


00:44:59.192 --> 00:45:01.160
No warning.


00:45:02.395 --> 00:45:05.990
He left a note saying
he hadn't signed up for this


00:45:06.032 --> 00:45:08.830
and we were holding him back.


00:45:10.904 --> 00:45:13.805
So you decided to date guys who
disappointed you at the start.


00:45:13.840 --> 00:45:15.831
Something like that.


00:45:17.777 --> 00:45:20.644
I so could have been that guy.


00:45:22.582 --> 00:45:24.743
(laughs)


00:45:26.653 --> 00:45:29.622
Oh man, you must think I'm crazy.


00:45:29.656 --> 00:45:31.556
Why are you still here?


00:45:31.591 --> 00:45:33.786
What is it about me?


00:45:35.295 --> 00:45:37.695
You're kind of like a good book
I can't put down yet.


00:45:43.603 --> 00:45:46.037
''It was one of those
rare smiles.


00:45:47.040 --> 00:45:49.304
It understood you just as you
wanted to be understood,


00:45:49.342 --> 00:45:52.573
and believed in you just as you
would like to believe in yourself


00:45:52.612 --> 00:45:54.443
and assured you
just the impression of yourself


00:45:54.480 --> 00:45:56.539
that you'd hope to convey.''


00:45:59.385 --> 00:46:01.285
Or something like that.


00:46:01.321 --> 00:46:03.289
(chuckles)


00:46:05.425 --> 00:46:07.484
So do you quote ''Gatsby''
to all the girls?


00:46:10.029 --> 00:46:11.360
(phone beeps)


00:46:11.397 --> 00:46:13.864
* Well, I've been lost
and I need direction *


00:46:13.899 --> 00:46:16.424
* And I could use
a little love protection *


00:46:16.468 --> 00:46:18.595
* What do you say, honey?
Come to my... *


00:46:18.637 --> 00:46:20.764
I have to go.


00:46:20.806 --> 00:46:23.969
After graduation my mom and I
are going to Europe for the summer.


00:46:24.009 --> 00:46:26.603
* I can take a punch,
I don't mind it bleeding *


00:46:26.645 --> 00:46:29.375
* As long as afterwards
you feel bad for me... *


00:46:29.414 --> 00:46:31.678
So do you think you'll be able
to live without me?


00:46:31.717 --> 00:46:34.208
I hope so.


00:46:34.252 --> 00:46:36.846
* I've got a deep desire
and it needs quenching *


00:46:36.888 --> 00:46:39.652
* And I think that's pretty plain
for you to see *


00:46:41.526 --> 00:46:44.552
* Well, enough about me
and more about you *


00:46:44.596 --> 00:46:47.292
* Would that be the gentlemanly
thing to do? *


00:46:47.332 --> 00:46:49.732
* I hope you like your men
sweet and polite... *


00:46:49.768 --> 00:46:53.204
So what is it about me?


00:46:53.238 --> 00:46:55.934
I don't know.
It's kind of hard to explain.


00:46:58.543 --> 00:47:00.943
It's like the rest of the world
is in black and white,


00:47:00.979 --> 00:47:03.709
you're in color.


00:47:03.749 --> 00:47:06.149
* Relationships, I don't know why *


00:47:06.184 --> 00:47:09.119
* They never work out,
they make you cry *


00:47:09.154 --> 00:47:12.453
* But the guy that says goodbye
to you is out of his mind. *


00:47:14.426 --> 00:47:14.493
(whirring)


00:47:14.493 --> 00:47:15.790
(whirring)


00:47:15.827 --> 00:47:18.193
(typing)


00:47:24.202 --> 00:47:26.170
Christ.


00:47:29.408 --> 00:47:31.433
(gasps)


00:47:33.311 --> 00:47:35.779
Just overrode the system.


00:47:35.814 --> 00:47:37.611
There's no way in hell
anyone or anything


00:47:37.649 --> 00:47:40.083
is getting in or out
of here before tonight.


00:47:40.118 --> 00:47:42.712
Just leave my money on the desk.


00:47:44.556 --> 00:47:46.421
Selling out your own species.


00:47:49.061 --> 00:47:50.619
How weak.


00:47:55.067 --> 00:47:56.830
Kathryn:
Will?


00:47:56.868 --> 00:47:58.699
Elliana?


00:48:01.506 --> 00:48:03.098
Elliana, is that you?


00:48:04.342 --> 00:48:07.607
Oh, it's you.
What are you doing here?


00:48:08.613 --> 00:48:10.581
I came here for you, Will.


00:48:13.485 --> 00:48:15.146
Holy shit.


00:48:16.321 --> 00:48:19.688
I've waited 18 years for this.


00:48:22.294 --> 00:48:24.159
It's time for us to go.


00:48:25.430 --> 00:48:27.660
What? Us?
Us go where?


00:48:28.934 --> 00:48:31.835
(laughs)


00:48:31.870 --> 00:48:33.929
Everywhere.


00:48:33.972 --> 00:48:35.701
(growling)


00:48:38.744 --> 00:48:40.302
You're one of them, aren't you?


00:48:40.345 --> 00:48:42.609
One of us.


00:48:50.722 --> 00:48:52.246
Hi, it's Sara Winter.


00:48:52.290 --> 00:48:54.417
Leave me a message
and I'll call you right back.


00:48:54.459 --> 00:48:56.324
- (beeps)
- Hey, Mom.


00:48:56.361 --> 00:48:58.329
I know you're probably on your way,


00:48:58.363 --> 00:49:01.457
but I was hoping we could
just meet after the ceremony.


00:49:01.500 --> 00:49:03.900
It's just there's this boy.


00:49:03.935 --> 00:49:06.096
And no, it's not Roland.


00:49:06.138 --> 00:49:08.766
I'd just really like to stay.


00:49:08.807 --> 00:49:11.503
I'm graduating today.
I can't believe it.


00:49:11.543 --> 00:49:13.841
All right, I love you, Mom.
Bye.


00:49:15.113 --> 00:49:16.512
(exhales)


00:49:17.816 --> 00:49:19.875
You survived an attack


00:49:21.720 --> 00:49:23.551
while you were still
in the womb.


00:49:26.591 --> 00:49:28.286
My womb.


00:49:32.531 --> 00:49:34.260
No.


00:49:34.299 --> 00:49:36.767
No, you died.
How are you even here?


00:49:36.802 --> 00:49:39.396
It's okay, honey.


00:49:39.437 --> 00:49:41.837
At first I was scared too.


00:49:41.873 --> 00:49:44.000
But just imagine


00:49:44.042 --> 00:49:48.103
having the power over all the things
you feel you can't control.


00:49:48.146 --> 00:49:49.943
It's amazing.


00:49:58.690 --> 00:50:00.248
Why did you wait so long?


00:50:01.593 --> 00:50:03.993
I was watching you,


00:50:04.029 --> 00:50:07.123
waiting until you were ready.


00:50:08.567 --> 00:50:10.262
And the blue moon.


00:50:10.302 --> 00:50:13.760
Tonight is gonna be so special.


00:50:14.806 --> 00:50:17.604
Wait wait. If I'm one of you, then why
are the other ones trying to kill me?


00:50:18.810 --> 00:50:20.209
(snarls)


00:50:20.245 --> 00:50:22.213
We weren't trying to kill you.


00:50:22.247 --> 00:50:24.647
We were trying to welcome you.


00:50:27.219 --> 00:50:29.483
So this curse--


00:50:29.521 --> 00:50:31.614
Gift.


00:50:31.656 --> 00:50:33.556
--has been inside me my whole life.


00:50:33.592 --> 00:50:36.823
You call this a life?


00:50:42.000 --> 00:50:43.900
Forget your books...


00:50:45.503 --> 00:50:46.731
and your technology.


00:50:50.709 --> 00:50:52.643
That's not life.


00:50:55.747 --> 00:50:58.511
It's a series of distractions
from life.


00:50:58.550 --> 00:51:01.917
Your father tried
to suppress you


00:51:01.953 --> 00:51:04.046
with drugs.


00:51:06.224 --> 00:51:09.660
He tried to domesticate you
like a yellow Lab.


00:51:09.694 --> 00:51:12.686
He taught you useless facts
and called it knowledge.


00:51:12.731 --> 00:51:15.029
He made you soft...


00:51:16.735 --> 00:51:18.726
and called it civilized.


00:51:25.977 --> 00:51:28.343
You have so much to learn.


00:51:28.380 --> 00:51:32.612
Life as you know it is over.


00:51:35.020 --> 00:51:37.215
Elliana:
You know, I thought about it,


00:51:37.255 --> 00:51:39.723
and I don't think you can
live without me.


00:51:39.758 --> 00:51:41.589
Will?


00:51:44.996 --> 00:51:46.395
Who's that?


00:51:47.399 --> 00:51:48.866
Uh...


00:51:48.900 --> 00:51:50.765
It's time for us to go, son.


00:51:53.672 --> 00:51:55.697
Son?


00:51:55.740 --> 00:51:59.073
Wait, I don't understand.
I thought your mom was dead.


00:52:07.852 --> 00:52:10.685
Listen, I thought about it
and I can definitely live without you.


00:52:16.094 --> 00:52:18.585
Goodbye.


00:52:18.630 --> 00:52:21.188
So what? I'm never gonna
see you again?


00:52:26.737 --> 00:52:29.228
Wait.


00:52:29.273 --> 00:52:31.537
What is going on here?


00:52:36.080 --> 00:52:38.446
Our use for you is over, pet.


00:52:40.417 --> 00:52:44.285
But you and me
can have a little fun


00:52:44.321 --> 00:52:46.186
before I put you out
of your misery.


00:52:46.223 --> 00:52:48.157
Jesus.


00:52:48.192 --> 00:52:50.183
He's not coming.


00:52:51.195 --> 00:52:54.562
Lesson number one, Will:
survival of the pack over all.


00:52:54.598 --> 00:52:58.329
Besides, we can't have anyone
knowing about us yet.


00:52:58.369 --> 00:52:59.961
It'd spoil the surprise.


00:53:08.145 --> 00:53:10.238
Hey!


00:53:17.721 --> 00:53:19.382
Let me do it.


00:53:19.423 --> 00:53:21.448
(laughs)


00:53:21.492 --> 00:53:23.517
Will?


00:53:23.560 --> 00:53:25.653
Please.


00:53:53.257 --> 00:53:55.487
(Elliana groans)


00:54:01.231 --> 00:54:02.994
Let him come to us.


00:54:08.338 --> 00:54:10.568
(coughs)


00:54:20.317 --> 00:54:22.683
(whimpers)


00:54:34.498 --> 00:54:36.090
Will.


00:54:37.935 --> 00:54:39.698
No, Will.


00:54:43.173 --> 00:54:45.403
(gasps)
Will.


00:54:47.478 --> 00:54:49.309
(cracking)


00:54:57.187 --> 00:54:59.314
(groaning)


00:55:00.357 --> 00:55:03.121
Will’s voice: You know what they say
about the white light?


00:55:03.160 --> 00:55:05.526
It's bullshit.


00:55:05.562 --> 00:55:07.962
Or maybe they just didn't
turn it on for me.


00:55:07.998 --> 00:55:10.558
What I did see


00:55:10.601 --> 00:55:13.832
was why the lure of immortality
is so strong.


00:55:16.640 --> 00:55:19.165
So you're--


00:55:20.978 --> 00:55:23.003
- A monster.
- (whimpers)


00:55:25.115 --> 00:55:27.174
Literally.


00:55:28.285 --> 00:55:30.120
(alarm sounding)


00:55:34.424 --> 00:55:37.222
Let's go.
Let's go before campus locks down.


00:55:48.672 --> 00:55:50.606
No! No!


00:56:00.284 --> 00:56:02.411
(lights humming)


00:56:06.890 --> 00:56:08.255
Elliana:
Now what?


00:56:09.259 --> 00:56:11.318
(gates clanging)


00:56:11.361 --> 00:56:12.953
(chugging)


00:56:14.598 --> 00:56:16.259
Okay.


00:56:17.267 --> 00:56:19.132
After tonight


00:56:19.169 --> 00:56:21.729
I will only return to this campus


00:56:21.772 --> 00:56:24.332
to promote my films


00:56:24.374 --> 00:56:26.899
and to autograph
women's breasts.


00:56:36.186 --> 00:56:38.746
Oh hi.
I didn't see you there.


00:56:38.789 --> 00:56:40.552
My name is Sachin.


00:56:40.591 --> 00:56:43.890
And you, ladies and gentlemen,
are about to witness


00:56:43.927 --> 00:56:47.260
the rebirth of American cinema.


00:56:47.297 --> 00:56:50.323
''Untitled Sachin Horror Project.''


00:56:50.367 --> 00:56:52.801
(door opening)


00:56:52.836 --> 00:56:54.326
(footsteps)


00:56:54.371 --> 00:56:56.134
Who's there?


00:56:56.173 --> 00:56:57.697
Man:
Sorry, Sachin.


00:56:57.741 --> 00:57:01.199
But this is where you fade to black.


00:57:01.245 --> 00:57:03.236
(growling)


00:57:04.715 --> 00:57:07.149
Oh, you've got to be kidding me.


00:57:10.954 --> 00:57:13.650
Please be there, security.
Security.


00:57:21.498 --> 00:57:23.762
Elliana:
Eddie?


00:57:23.800 --> 00:57:27.099
Keys. Where's his keys?
Where's his keys?


00:57:37.014 --> 00:57:39.039
Phones are dead.


00:57:40.083 --> 00:57:41.516
Uh...


00:57:44.288 --> 00:57:46.347
Okay, the school won't unlock
until after graduation.


00:57:46.390 --> 00:57:48.153
There has to be some sort
of override switch.


00:57:48.191 --> 00:57:50.682
Is there a chance anyone
is still on campus?


00:57:50.727 --> 00:57:52.354
(werewolf growling)


00:57:52.396 --> 00:57:54.125
(lights clattering)


00:57:54.164 --> 00:57:57.031
It's Sachin.
Sachin.


00:57:57.067 --> 00:57:59.399
Werewolfs on steroids!


00:57:59.436 --> 00:58:01.199
And they're so much more jacked up
than in the movies.


00:58:01.238 --> 00:58:04.207
They're not hiding in the woods, okay?
They're here.


00:58:04.241 --> 00:58:05.708
- (roars)
- God!


00:58:05.742 --> 00:58:08.404
Will, I'm so sorry
for not believing you, man.


00:58:08.445 --> 00:58:12.245
Look, whatever you do,
don't kill a human, okay?


00:58:12.282 --> 00:58:15.080
Once you do
there's no turning back.


00:58:15.118 --> 00:58:16.983
I'm about to die,
oh my God.


00:58:17.020 --> 00:58:21.218
Whoever finds this tape, please post it
on YouTube so I don't die in vain.


00:58:21.258 --> 00:58:23.453
(screaming)


00:58:23.493 --> 00:58:25.960
(werewolf growling)


00:58:35.404 --> 00:58:37.964
(thunder rumbles)


00:58:40.743 --> 00:58:42.870
- What are you doing?
- Protecting ourselves,


00:58:42.912 --> 00:58:45.938
assuming everything they taught us
in chemistry wasn't complete bullshit.


00:58:49.318 --> 00:58:51.582
Last night at the party there was
a hatch to the street.


00:58:51.620 --> 00:58:53.884
Maybe we can find it again from
the basement and get out of here.


00:58:58.461 --> 00:59:01.362
Thank you, Will,
for before.


00:59:02.631 --> 00:59:04.326
You would have done
the same for me.


00:59:08.537 --> 00:59:10.505
I'd like to think you'd have
done the same for me.


00:59:16.979 --> 00:59:18.970
Look, in case something happens,


00:59:19.014 --> 00:59:21.346
you think I never saw you,
but I did.


00:59:21.384 --> 00:59:24.478
I saw you drawing those pictures.


00:59:25.955 --> 00:59:28.947
You made me feel beautiful
on days that weren't.


00:59:31.494 --> 00:59:33.291
I could have said something
but I didn't


00:59:33.329 --> 00:59:37.561
because I thought whatever image
you had of me was better than who I was.


00:59:49.678 --> 00:59:51.270
What are we supposed
to do with that?


01:00:48.537 --> 01:00:50.562
(Elliana gasps)


01:01:31.614 --> 01:01:33.912
Elliana:
This can't be real.


01:01:38.988 --> 01:01:41.286
What are they doing
with all these people?


01:01:41.323 --> 01:01:44.224
How long have they been
collecting them?


01:01:49.164 --> 01:01:51.132
- (gasps)
- Elliana.


01:01:52.134 --> 01:01:55.297
Where's my light?
Where's my light? Where's my light?


01:01:58.274 --> 01:02:00.902
(whimpering)


01:02:02.478 --> 01:02:04.469
Kathryn:
Hello, son.


01:02:07.249 --> 01:02:11.515
Dad? What is this?
What's going on?


01:02:11.554 --> 01:02:15.513
He's outgrown his usefulness
to you, my boy.


01:02:15.558 --> 01:02:17.685
It's my turn.


01:02:19.128 --> 01:02:21.221
You're one of us now.


01:02:27.770 --> 01:02:29.829
Kill him.


01:02:32.007 --> 01:02:33.167
Do it!


01:02:37.613 --> 01:02:38.978
No.


01:02:41.817 --> 01:02:43.717
I'd rather die
than become one of you.


01:02:43.752 --> 01:02:45.686
Oh?


01:02:58.834 --> 01:03:00.734
- (cracks)
- No!


01:03:05.774 --> 01:03:09.073
Nothing and no one
can hold you back anymore.


01:03:09.111 --> 01:03:11.170
I'll never kill a human.


01:03:13.315 --> 01:03:14.714
But you already have.


01:03:18.621 --> 01:03:20.714
You killed Roland.


01:03:21.757 --> 01:03:25.693
I was there.
It was impressive.


01:03:27.162 --> 01:03:30.654
The only question is was it because
he was trying to kill you


01:03:30.699 --> 01:03:34.328
or because he had
something you wanted?


01:03:34.370 --> 01:03:36.497
Will?


01:03:48.117 --> 01:03:50.142
What have I done?


01:03:50.185 --> 01:03:52.415
You are your impulses now.


01:03:52.454 --> 01:03:55.912
No need to distinguish,
no need for control or guilt.


01:03:55.958 --> 01:03:58.927
Yeah.


01:03:58.961 --> 01:04:01.122
Just let go.


01:04:02.931 --> 01:04:05.229
Get out of here now.


01:04:05.267 --> 01:04:06.757
What about you?


01:04:06.802 --> 01:04:08.326
Just go!


01:04:08.370 --> 01:04:10.133
Wait for the campus
to unlock without me.


01:04:10.172 --> 01:04:12.538
- You can't stay here with them.
- It's none of your concern!


01:04:13.642 --> 01:04:15.803
Go. Go.


01:04:15.844 --> 01:04:19.075
Run away, little girl.


01:04:30.025 --> 01:04:32.288
Welcome to the family.


01:04:40.601 --> 01:04:42.762
What do you want to do first?


01:04:45.406 --> 01:04:47.670
(bottle clanks)


01:04:47.709 --> 01:04:50.644
Kill you.
Kill all of you.


01:04:52.180 --> 01:04:54.978
(growling)


01:04:55.016 --> 01:04:58.247
Will’s voice: Remember that mere 2%
that separates us from the animals?


01:04:58.286 --> 01:05:00.722
It's everything.


01:05:00.722 --> 01:05:02.781
(thunder rumbling)


01:05:02.824 --> 01:05:05.816
(cawing)


01:05:08.463 --> 01:05:11.432
- (howling)
- Will?


01:05:16.971 --> 01:05:19.166
Elliana?


01:05:19.207 --> 01:05:20.834
Elliana!


01:05:30.284 --> 01:05:32.445
Elliana?


01:05:33.855 --> 01:05:36.289
(whimpering)


01:05:41.362 --> 01:05:43.159
(stifled gasp)


01:05:47.869 --> 01:05:50.702
- (growls)
- (screaming)


01:05:50.738 --> 01:05:52.000
Elliana!


01:05:52.039 --> 01:05:54.303
No. No!


01:05:59.147 --> 01:06:01.479
(roars)


01:06:14.395 --> 01:06:17.330
(panting)


01:06:17.365 --> 01:06:19.993
I guess it's a good thing
you didn't win the gold.


01:06:23.704 --> 01:06:25.035
Will.


01:06:27.074 --> 01:06:29.167
Get away from me.


01:06:32.413 --> 01:06:34.711
They killed my dad.
They turned me into this.


01:06:34.749 --> 01:06:38.241
- You're not like them.
- Yes I am!


01:06:38.286 --> 01:06:39.981
- You have a choice.
- No I don't.


01:06:40.021 --> 01:06:42.785
You don't understand.
Every second I'm with you


01:06:42.824 --> 01:06:45.622
is about restraint, reining myself
in because the more I want you.


01:06:50.498 --> 01:06:51.692
Come on.


01:06:51.732 --> 01:06:54.394
Will’s voice: I've always been
scared of letting anyone in.


01:06:54.435 --> 01:06:57.871
Or maybe I've really been
scared of letting me out.


01:06:59.640 --> 01:07:01.972
Do what you want to do.


01:07:02.009 --> 01:07:03.636
What?


01:07:06.581 --> 01:07:09.778
Whatever it is, come on.


01:07:09.817 --> 01:07:11.944
Do it.


01:07:11.986 --> 01:07:14.045
Come on.


01:07:17.925 --> 01:07:19.916
You don't know what you're saying.


01:07:19.961 --> 01:07:23.021
Come on, Will.
Let's go.


01:07:25.132 --> 01:07:26.724
Let it happen.


01:07:26.767 --> 01:07:29.099
* Come on, baby *


01:07:29.136 --> 01:07:31.161
* Don't fear the reaper *


01:07:31.205 --> 01:07:33.639
* Take my hand *


01:07:33.674 --> 01:07:35.164
* Don't fear the reaper... *


01:07:35.209 --> 01:07:36.733
Are you sure?


01:07:36.777 --> 01:07:38.472
* We'll be able to fly *


01:07:38.512 --> 01:07:40.480
* Don't fear the reaper *


01:07:40.514 --> 01:07:42.812
* Baby, I'm your man *


01:07:42.850 --> 01:07:45.375
* Don't fear the reaper *


01:07:45.419 --> 01:07:47.250
* Baby, I'm your man *


01:07:47.288 --> 01:07:49.722
* La la la *


01:07:49.757 --> 01:07:52.282
* La la... *


01:07:56.464 --> 01:07:58.261
Get away from me.


01:07:58.299 --> 01:08:00.597
Did you ever think maybe if I was
like you that I could help you?


01:08:00.635 --> 01:08:03.365
- Maybe we could be a team.
- You think you could save me?


01:08:03.404 --> 01:08:05.235
Huh?
Is that what you want to do?


01:08:05.273 --> 01:08:07.400
If you don't want
to be with me, just say it.


01:08:07.441 --> 01:08:10.877
That's not what I'm saying.
I just can't. You don't want this.


01:08:10.912 --> 01:08:14.780
Don't tell me what I want.


01:08:14.815 --> 01:08:17.010
What are you so afraid of?


01:08:17.051 --> 01:08:20.384
Or maybe the better question is
what aren't you afraid of?


01:08:20.421 --> 01:08:23.219
You've been living
in your safe little world


01:08:23.257 --> 01:08:24.884
where everybody
tells you what to do


01:08:24.926 --> 01:08:27.121
and you're too scared
to do anything about it.


01:08:27.161 --> 01:08:28.753
Yeah well, you're afraid
that you're gonna die


01:08:28.796 --> 01:08:30.696
so I'm just another guy who's safe
to be with for the moment


01:08:30.731 --> 01:08:32.323
because it has zero chances
of working out.


01:08:32.366 --> 01:08:34.926
I'm asking you
to make me like you.


01:08:34.969 --> 01:08:37.335
How much more of a commitment
do you need?


01:08:39.607 --> 01:08:44.044
I think you're afraid that if you
love me, I won't love you back.


01:08:46.013 --> 01:08:49.380
Yeah well, maybe you're afraid
that I will.


01:08:49.417 --> 01:08:51.248
Try me.


01:08:51.285 --> 01:08:53.549
* We can be like they are *


01:08:53.587 --> 01:08:55.851
* So come on, baby *


01:08:55.890 --> 01:08:58.552
* Don't fear the reaper... *


01:08:58.592 --> 01:08:59.786
(grunts)


01:08:59.827 --> 01:09:02.796
* La la la *


01:09:02.830 --> 01:09:04.889
* La la... *


01:09:04.932 --> 01:09:07.628
- (moans)
- (heart beating)


01:09:08.636 --> 01:09:11.799
* La la la *


01:09:11.839 --> 01:09:14.137
* La la... *


01:09:14.175 --> 01:09:16.735
Ah!


01:09:16.777 --> 01:09:18.677
* Take my hand *


01:09:18.713 --> 01:09:20.874
* Don't fear the reaper *


01:09:20.915 --> 01:09:22.610
* We'll be able to fly... *


01:09:22.650 --> 01:09:24.982
Leave me alone!


01:09:25.019 --> 01:09:27.647
* Baby, I'm your man *


01:09:30.591 --> 01:09:32.422
* Baby, I'm your man... *


01:09:32.460 --> 01:09:34.587
I'm so sorry.


01:09:38.466 --> 01:09:40.696
I won't be the one who hurts you.


01:09:42.036 --> 01:09:45.767
I told you, you have a choice.


01:09:45.806 --> 01:09:48.502
You don't have to kill again.
You know that, right?


01:09:48.542 --> 01:09:50.806
Will’s voice:
My generation,


01:09:50.845 --> 01:09:52.972
we're not about commitments
and relationships.


01:09:53.014 --> 01:09:55.107
We're about hooking up.


01:09:55.149 --> 01:09:58.016
It's like somewhere along the way
we were led to believe


01:09:58.052 --> 01:10:02.455
that knowing too much about a partner
somehow makes love less exciting.


01:10:03.758 --> 01:10:06.022
We were led to believe wrong.


01:10:06.060 --> 01:10:08.028
Kathryn on P.A.:
Attention please.


01:10:08.062 --> 01:10:10.292
Would Will Kidman
and the campus whore


01:10:10.331 --> 01:10:12.799
please report
to the principal's office?


01:10:12.833 --> 01:10:15.666
Thank you.


01:10:15.703 --> 01:10:17.967
Come on, we have
to get to the chapel.


01:10:22.009 --> 01:10:24.500
You came from inside of me, my son.


01:10:24.545 --> 01:10:27.715
That's a fact and you'd better start
learning how to deal with it.


01:10:29.283 --> 01:10:30.341
We have to throw off their scent.


01:10:30.384 --> 01:10:32.318
Kathryn:
There's no use fighting it.


01:10:32.353 --> 01:10:34.651
Push me away,
I'll tighten my grip.


01:10:34.688 --> 01:10:36.849
It's what mothers do.


01:10:36.891 --> 01:10:39.916
The world as you know it
is about to change.


01:10:41.394 --> 01:10:45.694
500 years ago
people knew the Earth was flat.


01:10:50.570 --> 01:10:52.731
This morning everybody knew


01:10:52.772 --> 01:10:55.070
that humans were at
the top of the food chain.


01:11:00.013 --> 01:11:03.847
My boy, that isn't food below.


01:11:06.386 --> 01:11:08.047
It's an army.


01:11:09.589 --> 01:11:12.558
It's coming to life as we speak.


01:11:12.592 --> 01:11:15.026
And tonight
when the blue moon rises,


01:11:15.061 --> 01:11:17.586
we will lead this world
into a new era.


01:11:23.703 --> 01:11:26.331
Roland's gun.


01:11:27.574 --> 01:11:29.542
(werewolf growling)


01:11:35.915 --> 01:11:39.009
(thunder crashing)


01:11:44.891 --> 01:11:47.382
Hollow points. Perfect.


01:11:53.233 --> 01:11:55.292
Argentum nitricum?


01:11:55.335 --> 01:11:57.394
AKA silver nitrate.


01:12:00.039 --> 01:12:01.939
We have to warn people what's
happening before it's too late.


01:12:01.975 --> 01:12:04.569
We can use the broadcast hack
Sachin set up.


01:12:04.611 --> 01:12:06.010
They won't believe us.


01:12:06.045 --> 01:12:07.535
They'll think it's just a couple
of kids playing a joke.


01:12:07.580 --> 01:12:08.911
That's why we have to
make them believe.


01:12:08.948 --> 01:12:10.813
How?


01:12:13.653 --> 01:12:15.678
I'm gonna turn into one.


01:12:17.690 --> 01:12:19.521
You might need this


01:12:21.327 --> 01:12:24.091
in case I'm not strong enough
to come back.


01:12:29.302 --> 01:12:30.599
Let's do this.


01:12:31.804 --> 01:12:34.238
I don't want to lose you,


01:12:34.274 --> 01:12:37.710
even though I feel like I've been
seriously damaged


01:12:37.744 --> 01:12:39.644
by this relationship.


01:12:39.679 --> 01:12:41.977
(both laugh)


01:12:47.820 --> 01:12:49.651
It's graduation time.


01:12:49.689 --> 01:12:52.453
(''Pomp and Circumstance''
playing)


01:13:11.544 --> 01:13:13.409
(exhales)


01:13:20.553 --> 01:13:23.386
Hey hey.
Hey, look.


01:13:25.158 --> 01:13:29.219
I need you to be strong
and stay with me


01:13:29.262 --> 01:13:32.493
because you're the one


01:13:32.532 --> 01:13:34.966
who's gonna have to kill me.


01:13:37.203 --> 01:13:41.037
* I will keep the bad things
from you *


01:13:41.074 --> 01:13:45.408
* I will love you
like no other *


01:13:45.445 --> 01:13:49.176
* I will be your dad and mother *


01:13:49.215 --> 01:13:53.117
* I will give you older brothers *


01:13:53.152 --> 01:13:57.111
* I will keep your smile
from falling *


01:13:57.156 --> 01:14:01.149
* I will keep the price
below cost *


01:14:01.194 --> 01:14:05.597
* I will lead the way
when all is lost *


01:14:09.002 --> 01:14:10.697
* Catch it while you can *


01:14:10.737 --> 01:14:14.002
* It's the feel-good hit
of the summer *


01:14:17.310 --> 01:14:18.937
* Catch it while you can *


01:14:18.978 --> 01:14:22.744
* 'Cause there won't be another *


01:14:22.782 --> 01:14:27.276
* Won't be another *


01:14:29.722 --> 01:14:33.021
* I will keep the bad things
from you. *


01:14:34.227 --> 01:14:35.922
(beeping)


01:14:35.962 --> 01:14:38.055
Sorry, Will.


01:14:38.097 --> 01:14:40.895
The evolution will not be televised.


01:14:43.903 --> 01:14:45.734
Who the hell are you


01:14:45.772 --> 01:14:47.706
to warn people about us?


01:14:52.378 --> 01:14:54.869
Fellow graduates,


01:14:54.914 --> 01:14:57.712
let's not let it rain on our parade.


01:15:03.156 --> 01:15:04.919
I want to love you.


01:15:04.957 --> 01:15:08.188
Really, I do.


01:15:09.796 --> 01:15:12.492
But you're making it so


01:15:12.532 --> 01:15:16.298
incredibly difficult.


01:15:18.404 --> 01:15:21.601
We admit it, we're scared.


01:15:21.641 --> 01:15:25.202
We always hear how there's still
so many things that we don't know,


01:15:25.244 --> 01:15:28.475
but I'd like to think that we know
more than you think.


01:15:29.849 --> 01:15:32.443
We just haven't summoned it yet.


01:15:32.485 --> 01:15:35.249
Why would you even try
to save those people?


01:15:35.288 --> 01:15:38.917
Those people that have made your life
nothing but miserable all these years?


01:15:40.560 --> 01:15:42.619
Because I'm not like you.


01:15:51.337 --> 01:15:53.532
Imagine how disappointed I am


01:15:53.573 --> 01:15:56.303
after 18 years to find out you're...


01:15:58.344 --> 01:16:00.437
so ordinary.


01:16:00.480 --> 01:16:04.007
Imagine how disappointed
I am to find out that you're not.


01:16:04.050 --> 01:16:06.917
Certainly there are lessons
yet to be learned


01:16:06.953 --> 01:16:08.682
as we leave high school behind.


01:16:08.721 --> 01:16:12.316
But let me share with you
a few I've learned already.


01:16:14.227 --> 01:16:17.526
Clearly the girl has clouded
your judgment.


01:16:17.563 --> 01:16:20.293
You might not thank me now
for getting rid of her,


01:16:20.333 --> 01:16:22.324
but trust me,


01:16:22.368 --> 01:16:23.733
one day you will.


01:16:26.739 --> 01:16:28.866
Never look back.


01:16:28.908 --> 01:16:30.705
Behind you!


01:16:30.743 --> 01:16:33.075
- (gunshot)
- (roars)


01:16:33.112 --> 01:16:35.137
That which doesn't kill us


01:16:35.181 --> 01:16:38.708
- makes us stronger.
- (grunts)


01:16:38.751 --> 01:16:42.346
At the end of every dark tunnel
is a light.


01:16:43.956 --> 01:16:46.355
(roars)


01:16:48.927 --> 01:16:51.828
When one door closes,
another opens.


01:16:58.537 --> 01:17:00.505
- Come on.
- (growling)


01:17:08.814 --> 01:17:11.476
Elliana, come on.
Come on, Elliana.


01:17:15.654 --> 01:17:19.112
We've come this far.
Come on, Elliana, come on!


01:17:22.127 --> 01:17:24.687
Come on, don't go.
Don't go.


01:17:24.729 --> 01:17:26.788
Don't go!


01:17:28.633 --> 01:17:30.362
Wake up!
Come on!


01:17:31.870 --> 01:17:33.895
Come on, fight.


01:17:42.047 --> 01:17:45.380
Come on, Elliana.
Breathe. Breathe!


01:17:47.586 --> 01:17:49.383
Come on.
Come on.


01:17:51.523 --> 01:17:54.390
You'd never let go.
Don't you dare let go.


01:18:00.665 --> 01:18:03.156
I can't live without you, Elliana.
Come on.


01:18:03.201 --> 01:18:04.759
Come on, Elliana.


01:18:08.640 --> 01:18:10.801
(gasps)


01:18:16.014 --> 01:18:18.414
- Hi.
- You're alive.


01:18:21.052 --> 01:18:24.044
- (screams)
- No!


01:18:24.089 --> 01:18:26.216
Will Kidman.


01:18:29.261 --> 01:18:31.491
Will Kidman?


01:18:41.973 --> 01:18:43.702
(gunshot)


01:18:43.742 --> 01:18:46.336
(werewolf howling)


01:18:53.985 --> 01:18:56.886
Elliana!


01:18:56.922 --> 01:18:59.015
Elliana Winter.


01:19:01.026 --> 01:19:03.256
Elliana Winter?


01:19:07.365 --> 01:19:09.799
Elliana!
Elliana!


01:19:14.005 --> 01:19:16.565
Ladies and gentlemen,
I give you


01:19:16.608 --> 01:19:19.076
this year's graduating class.


01:19:19.110 --> 01:19:21.874
(cheering, applauding)


01:19:25.383 --> 01:19:27.078
Bravo, Will.


01:19:27.118 --> 01:19:29.211
You've got more potential
than I thought.


01:19:29.254 --> 01:19:32.553
You're alive. How?


01:19:32.591 --> 01:19:34.650
Oh, honey,


01:19:34.693 --> 01:19:38.094
it's gonna take a lot more
than a little fire to get rid of me.


01:19:38.129 --> 01:19:40.097
It's a cruel world


01:19:40.131 --> 01:19:44.261
and the only morality in a cruel world
is every being for themselves.


01:19:44.302 --> 01:19:47.999
Even if you win this battle,
you lose the war.


01:19:48.039 --> 01:19:51.440
There are thousands of other armies
out there just like ours.


01:19:51.476 --> 01:19:54.206
So why resist?
There's nothing you can do.


01:19:54.245 --> 01:19:56.076
I know it's hard to swallow.


01:19:59.384 --> 01:20:01.352
Swallow this!


01:20:02.854 --> 01:20:05.322
(coughing, gagging)


01:20:09.561 --> 01:20:11.028
(swallows)


01:20:11.062 --> 01:20:13.257
(laughs)


01:20:13.298 --> 01:20:15.232
(growls)


01:20:15.266 --> 01:20:17.461
You're the alpha.


01:20:17.502 --> 01:20:19.834
You're damn right I am.


01:20:21.339 --> 01:20:24.308
And now I'm gonna do to you what
I should have done 18 years ago--


01:20:26.478 --> 01:20:28.070
abort you.


01:20:29.714 --> 01:20:31.272
Why?


01:20:31.316 --> 01:20:33.477
'Cause your boy likes his girlfriend
better than Mommy?


01:20:33.518 --> 01:20:35.816
(growling)


01:20:40.091 --> 01:20:41.490
(grunts)


01:20:43.795 --> 01:20:45.524
(roars)


01:20:49.000 --> 01:20:51.332
What, you jealous?
You pissed off?


01:20:51.369 --> 01:20:53.303
Hell, that makes you
the most human one here.


01:20:53.338 --> 01:20:54.965
(roars)


01:20:56.174 --> 01:20:57.732
(grunts)


01:21:03.281 --> 01:21:06.682
(heart beating)


01:21:06.718 --> 01:21:08.811
(groaning)


01:21:13.992 --> 01:21:16.552
(growling)


01:21:21.866 --> 01:21:24.391
(growling, roaring)


01:22:45.250 --> 01:22:45.283
(growling)


01:22:45.283 --> 01:22:47.615
(growling)


01:22:54.158 --> 01:22:57.093
Go ahead.
Put me out of your misery.


01:22:58.996 --> 01:23:01.556
(shrieks)


01:23:04.968 --> 01:23:06.731
(growls)


01:23:18.782 --> 01:23:20.613
(growling)


01:23:23.153 --> 01:23:24.643
Will:
What have I done?


01:23:33.430 --> 01:23:34.920
Elliana?


01:23:36.834 --> 01:23:39.098
You're in there somewhere.


01:23:39.136 --> 01:23:40.865
It's hard.


01:23:40.904 --> 01:23:44.169
I know what you're feeling.


01:23:44.208 --> 01:23:46.836
So if you can't come back,


01:23:46.877 --> 01:23:48.344
then kill me.


01:23:48.378 --> 01:23:51.939
Because the only way I'm walking
out of here is together.


01:23:51.982 --> 01:23:54.746
But you have a choice.


01:23:54.785 --> 01:23:57.754
You know that, right?


01:23:57.788 --> 01:23:59.756
Come on.


01:24:26.416 --> 01:24:27.849
(heart beating)


01:24:43.267 --> 01:24:45.531
Here.


01:24:47.371 --> 01:24:49.635
(laughs)


01:24:50.674 --> 01:24:52.665
Will.


01:25:19.269 --> 01:25:20.998
* The book of love *


01:25:21.038 --> 01:25:23.905
* Is long and boring *


01:25:23.941 --> 01:25:26.705
* No one can lift *


01:25:26.743 --> 01:25:29.371
* The damn thing *


01:25:29.413 --> 01:25:32.109
* It's full of charts *


01:25:32.149 --> 01:25:35.676
* And facts and figures *


01:25:35.719 --> 01:25:39.951
* And instructions
for dancing *


01:25:39.990 --> 01:25:45.428
* But I *


01:25:45.462 --> 01:25:47.987
* I love it *


01:25:48.031 --> 01:25:50.932
* When you read to me *


01:25:50.968 --> 01:25:56.531
* And you *


01:25:57.541 --> 01:26:01.637
* You can read me anything *


01:26:03.180 --> 01:26:07.139
* The book of love
has music in it *


01:26:08.285 --> 01:26:12.745
* In fact, that's where
music comes from... *


01:26:12.789 --> 01:26:14.620
Will's voice:
Most of us don't have the option


01:26:14.658 --> 01:26:18.150
of waking to eternal life
or experiencing undying romance.


01:26:18.195 --> 01:26:20.993
Our lives and loves
are painfully finite.


01:26:25.535 --> 01:26:28.026
But maybe that's how it should be.


01:26:28.071 --> 01:26:31.598
Because the parts of the human
condition that we suffer from most


01:26:31.641 --> 01:26:34.542
are the very things
that make us what we are.


01:26:34.578 --> 01:26:38.446
* And you... *


01:26:38.482 --> 01:26:40.848
Will’s voice: We appreciate time
because of our lack of it.


01:26:40.884 --> 01:26:44.376
* You can sing me anything *


01:26:45.922 --> 01:26:47.480
* The book of love... *


01:26:47.524 --> 01:26:51.290
Will’s voice: We're sensitive
because of our vulnerability.


01:26:51.328 --> 01:26:54.024
We're compassionate
because of our dependence.


01:26:56.733 --> 01:26:58.360
* It's full of flowers... *


01:26:58.402 --> 01:27:01.337
Will’s voice:
And while we can all be monsters...


01:27:01.371 --> 01:27:06.399
* And things we're all
too young to know... *


01:27:08.412 --> 01:27:10.539
Will’s voice:
...we're always at our most monstrous


01:27:10.580 --> 01:27:12.343
when we ignore our humanity.


01:27:25.896 --> 01:27:28.592
(roaring, howling)


01:27:31.568 --> 01:27:33.433
(window shatters)


01:27:33.470 --> 01:27:35.267
(bodies thud)


01:27:35.305 --> 01:27:39.241
(students murmuring)


01:27:39.276 --> 01:27:42.712
- (explosion)
- (students screaming)


01:27:44.448 --> 01:27:46.416
Will’s voice:
Our teachers and parents like to say


01:27:46.450 --> 01:27:49.180
we're witnessing the decline
of Western civilization.


01:27:49.219 --> 01:27:52.120
Sure, these are trying times.


01:27:52.155 --> 01:27:55.921
But when we begin to lose ourselves
in routine or fear or tragedy,


01:27:55.959 --> 01:27:58.359
I think we can always
find our way back.


01:27:58.395 --> 01:28:01.626
We just need to remember
that our obligations to one another,


01:28:01.665 --> 01:28:04.327
our relationships to one another,


01:28:04.367 --> 01:28:07.131
these things don't exist
only to fill up our days.


01:28:07.170 --> 01:28:09.604
They exist to save our lives.


01:28:09.639 --> 01:28:11.971
And these things
are worth fighting for.


01:28:13.510 --> 01:28:15.569
''It's a whole new world.''


01:28:15.612 --> 01:28:18.206
''The future begins here.''


01:28:18.248 --> 01:28:20.148
(chuckles)


01:28:20.183 --> 01:28:23.243
You people have no fucking idea.


01:28:26.022 --> 01:28:28.820
* You are to give me *


01:28:28.859 --> 01:28:32.090
* A wedding ring. *


01:28:35.499 --> 01:28:37.490
(growling)


01:28:37.534 --> 01:28:40.094
- Two three four.
- (rock music playing)


01:28:46.576 --> 01:28:48.544
Will: I need you to be strong
and stay with me...


01:28:48.578 --> 01:28:51.638
Hey, man, do you think this is real?


01:28:51.681 --> 01:28:54.377
...because you're the one


01:28:54.417 --> 01:28:56.408
who's going to have to kill me.


01:28:56.453 --> 01:29:01.014
Nah, it looks like viral marketing
for some movie.


01:29:02.925 --> 01:29:05.655
* It never really costs that much *


01:29:05.694 --> 01:29:08.458
* If you consider the return... *


01:29:08.497 --> 01:29:12.957
Will on TV: And now, 18 years
after the day I was born,


01:29:13.002 --> 01:29:16.961
I'm here to convince you
that the monsters are real,


01:29:17.006 --> 01:29:19.133
that they live among us,


01:29:19.175 --> 01:29:21.336
within us.


01:29:21.377 --> 01:29:25.006
And hopefully one day
you'll know who I was


01:29:25.047 --> 01:29:26.878
and what I tried to do.


01:29:26.916 --> 01:29:32.047
* And it's my favorite revolution *


01:29:33.055 --> 01:29:38.357
* It's my favorite revolution *


01:29:38.394 --> 01:29:41.830
* It's my favorite *


01:29:41.864 --> 01:29:43.491
* Favorite *


01:29:43.532 --> 01:29:47.229
* Favorite revolution... *


01:29:50.039 --> 01:29:52.974
Will on TV:
Please listen to me.


01:29:53.008 --> 01:29:56.535
I need you to gather
all the silver and fire...


01:29:56.579 --> 01:29:58.774
(breathing heavily)


01:29:58.814 --> 01:30:02.443
...and kill them
before it's too late.


01:30:02.484 --> 01:30:04.884
- (people screaming)
- (roars)


01:30:04.920 --> 01:30:08.151
* Revolution *


01:30:18.167 --> 01:30:20.795
* Now it's all updated *


01:30:20.836 --> 01:30:24.135
* Plastic and laser beams... *


01:30:24.173 --> 01:30:25.800
Reporter:
Police stations and authorities


01:30:25.841 --> 01:30:27.502
are being flooded with werewolf--


01:30:27.543 --> 01:30:30.603
yes, werewolf-- sightings
on four continents.


01:30:30.646 --> 01:30:33.240
Officials are currently
assessing the situation


01:30:33.282 --> 01:30:37.150
and asking people to stay indoors
until further notice.


01:30:37.186 --> 01:30:40.622
* I'll make you famous,
sweet revenge *


01:30:40.656 --> 01:30:42.556
* Will come in time *


01:30:42.591 --> 01:30:45.389
* Where would we be without them? *


01:30:45.427 --> 01:30:48.191
* Thank God we'll never know *


01:30:48.230 --> 01:30:51.324
* We're safe and sound
as angels *


01:30:51.367 --> 01:30:54.336
* When it's loud we dance slow *


01:30:54.370 --> 01:30:59.433
* And it's my favorite revolution... *


01:31:00.776 --> 01:31:02.141
Reporter:
People are panicking,


01:31:02.177 --> 01:31:03.974
gathering silver and firearms


01:31:04.013 --> 01:31:07.107
as military troops around the globe
are mobilizing.


01:31:07.149 --> 01:31:10.880
(static)
...attacks leaving thousands of victims.


01:31:10.919 --> 01:31:14.878
* Favorite revolution... *


01:31:29.004 --> 01:31:31.837
(werewolves howling)


01:31:40.115 --> 01:31:45.610
* It's my favorite revolution *


01:31:46.622 --> 01:31:49.182
* It's my favorite *


01:31:49.224 --> 01:31:50.816
* Favorite *


01:31:50.859 --> 01:31:52.554
* Favorite... *


01:31:52.594 --> 01:31:55.028
Do you believe us now?


01:31:55.064 --> 01:31:58.363
* Drop the needle,
there's a song to be sung *


01:31:58.400 --> 01:32:00.334
* When the tables turn, baby *


01:32:00.369 --> 01:32:04.601
* It's my favorite revolution. *

